                                        <div class="tab-pane fade active show" id="pills-1" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="Introduction"><p>The Planning and Development Division was established in the Year 1987-88. The Division is principal Planning unit engaged in formulating short-term and long-term plans, policies, and procedures to operationalize various programmes and activities of the University. It periodically reviews and monitors the performance of all the schemes and activities of the University. Management Information System (MIS) of the university is housed in the Division. The Division periodically publish reports/Books highlighting progress/achievements of the University.<p>The Division coordinates in facilitating design, development and delivery of academic programmes /activities, its procedures, administrative reforms, students support network in order to improve quality of the Open and Distance Education. The Division acts as secretariat for the Planning Board (PB), a statutory body of the University, and its Standing Committee i.e. the Academic Programme Committee (APC).</p></p></div>

                                        
                                    </div>
                                    <div>
                                        

                                        <div class="tab-pane fade" id="pills-2" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="Director&#39;sMessage"  ><p>Welcome to the Planning and Development Division (P&amp;DD) of Indira Gandhi National
Open University. Since its establishment in 1987–88, the Division has been the principal
planning unit of the University, guiding its vision, policies, and growth strategies in the field
of Open and Distance Learning (ODL).</p>
<p>Our mission is to ensure that IGNOU’s programmes and activities remain learner-centric,
innovative, and socially relevant. We prepare and monitor the University’s short-term and
long-term plans, strengthen academic and administrative systems, and coordinate the design
and delivery of programmes to enhance the quality of ODL.</p>
<p>AThe Division plays a pivotal role in preparing and monitoring the University’s strategic plans,
and special initiatives such as the Scheduled Caste and Tribal Sub-Plans. It undertakes
research, data analysis, and impact studies to inform policies, evaluates proposals for new
academic programmes, and supports review and audit processes to ensure quality. The
Division also oversees budgeting and cost analysis, coordinates externally funded projects
and collaborations. P&amp;DD serves as a nodal unit for data collection, analysis, and reporting to
support evidence-based decision-making and national surveys like AISHE.</p>
<p>In addition, the Division functions as the secretariat to the Planning Board (PB), the
University’s apex planning body, and its Standing Committee (Academic Programme
Committee (APC)). Together, we evaluate new academic initiatives, optimize resources, and
guide IGNOU’s developmental priorities.</p>
<p>As we look ahead, the Planning and Development Division remains committed to excellence,
inclusivity, and innovation, ensuring that IGNOU continues to be a global leader in open,
distance and online learning.</p>
<p>Warm regards,<br/>Prof. V.V. Subrahmanyam<br/>(Director (I/C)<br/>Planning &amp; Development Division<br/>Indira Gandhi National Open University (IGNOU), Delhi</p></div>
